# mm.fs.littlefs

littlefs on a FlashDevice: a power-loss resilient, wear-levelled file system
for raw flash, mounted at a prefix. mount answers Corrupt for a device that
holds no littlefs volume and never erases it; format writes an empty volume
over the whole device. mm.fs.local on a Pico is this, on the flash region,
formatting a region that was never written.

The Pico SDKs bind platform.pico.fs.littlefs, which runs littlefs compiled by
the Pico bridge. A program reaching mm.fs.littlefs is unavailable on a lane
that binds no provider; with none bound the fallback answers Unsupported.
unmount detaches only volumes this module attached.
